Description: Store runtime state under /var/lib instead of /etc
 The sysfs "original values" file is runtime state written by the daemon, not
 configuration: it records the pre-tuning values of the resource nodes so they
 can be restored after an unclean shutdown. Per Debian Policy 9.1.1 that is
 variable data and belongs under /var/lib, not /etc.
 .
 Besides the layout violation, the old location never worked. Nothing created
 /etc/urm/data/, and AuxRoutines::writeToFile() does not create parent
 directories, so the write silently failed and restoreToSafeState() found no
 file on the next start. Resource nodes were therefore left at whatever URM
 last wrote them after a crash or SIGKILL.
 .
 Point the file at /var/lib/urm/, which the package now ships via a tmpfiles
 snippet, so persistence and the restore-on-startup path actually take effect.
Author: Lukas Märdian <lukas.maerdian@oss.qualcomm.com>
Forwarded: https://github.com/qualcomm/userspace-resource-manager/pull/283
Last-Update: 2026-08-11

